@startuml Dynamic Asset Flow - Simplified
!theme plain
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam BoxPadding 20

title Dynamic Asset Addition - Simplified Flow

box "Asset Creation" #LightBlue
  actor Admin
  participant "GraphQL API" as API
  participant "Organization\nService" as Org
end box

box "Storage & Signing" #LightGreen
  database "Special Org\n(ASSET_SUPPORT_V2)" as SpecialOrg
  participant "HSM" as HSM
end box

box "Asset Registry Service" #LightYellow
  participant "Cron Job\n(60s)" as Cron
  database "Database" as DB
end box

box "Client Services" #LightPink
  participant "AssetTypes\nClient (10s)" as Client
  database "Cache" as Cache
  participant "Services" as Services
end box

== 1. Asset Addition & Approval ==

Admin -> API: Add Asset Support\n(name, network, decimals, etc.)
API -> Org: Create organization change

Org -> HSM: Sign organization with new asset
HSM --> SpecialOrg: Store signed organization ✓

== 2. Asset Registry Sync ==

Cron -> SpecialOrg: Get special org (every 60s)
SpecialOrg --> Cron: Return all AssetConfigs
Cron -> DB: Upsert asset records
note right
  Stores asset metadata:
  name, decimals, networkID, etc.
end note

== 3. Client Cache Population ==

Client -> DB: ListAssetTypes gRPC (every 10s)
DB --> Client: Return asset list
Client -> Cache: Update in-memory cache
note right
  Maps assetTypeID -> AssetInfo
  Triggers callbacks for consumers
end note

== 4. Service Usage ==

Services -> Client: Get asset info by ID
Client -> Cache: Lookup in cache
Cache --> Client: Return AssetInfo
Client --> Services: Asset details available

@enduml
